  "source": "research:chains-beverage",
  "note": "Beverage, dessert and bakery chains in Malaysia. NOTHING here is verified, and the reason is worth recording: every Malaysian chain that genuinely publishes a panel is unreachable. starbucks.com.my, krispykreme.com.my and baskinrobbins.com sit behind a Cloudflare bot challenge; ZUS Coffee, Tealive, Chatime, Gong Cha, Chagee, Bask Bear and Coffee Bean publish calories only inside their ordering apps and have no nutrition page on the public site (checked their sitemaps and WordPress page indexes). So the sourcing is in three tiers. `chain_menu_my` is a Malaysian menu item costed from its known composition and the calorie figures the chain circulates — an estimate, not a transcription. `*_us_nutrition_*_not_malaysian` / `*_es_*` rows are the same item's published panel from a market that does publish, which is real data about a different country's recipe. `model_estimate` is the bakery counters, where nobody publishes anywhere. Drink sizes are written into the serving label because a Regular and a Large are different foods to a diary; `extra_servings` carries the other cup where the ratio is clean.",
